{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Solution {\n    static BufferedReader reader;\n    static StringTokenizer tokenizer;\n    static PrintWriter writer;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        writer = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        solve();\n        writer.flush();\n    }\n\n    static void solve() throws IOException {\n        int a = nextInt();\n        int b = nextInt();\n        int l = nextInt() - 1;\n        int r = nextInt() - 1;\n        int len = r - l + 1;\n\n        int best = len;\n\n        for (char x = 'a'; x <= 'z'; x++) {\n            for (char y = 'a'; y <= 'z'; y++) {\n                for (char z = 'a'; z <= 'z'; z++) {\n                    char[] pattern = {x, y, z};\n                    best = Math.min(best, calculateDistinct(a, b, l, r, pattern));\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        writer.println(best);\n    }\n\n    static int calculateDistinct(int a, int b, int L, int R, char[] pat) {\n        int period = a + b;\n        char[] base = new char[3 * period];\n        \n        for (int idx = 0; idx < 3; idx++) {\n            System.arraycopy(generatePrefix(base, idx * period, a), 0, base, idx * period, a);\n            Arrays.fill(base, idx * period + a, (idx + 1) * period, pat[idx]);\n        }\n\n        int start = L % period;\n        int windowSize = R - L + 1;\n        char[] segment = new char[windowSize];\n        System.arraycopy(base, start, segment, 0, Math.min(windowSize, base.length - start));\n\n        boolean[] seen = new boolean[26];\n        for (char c : segment) seen[c - 'a'] = true;\n\n        int distinct = 0;\n        for (boolean s : seen) if (s) distinct++;\n\n        return distinct;\n    }\n\n    static char[] generatePrefix(char[] buffer, int offset, int length) {\n        boolean[] used = new boolean[26];\n        for (int i = offset - 1; i >= offset - length && i >= 0; i--) {\n            used[buffer[i] - 'a'] = true;\n        }\n\n        char[] res = new char[length];\n        char current = 'a';\n        for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\n            while (used[current - 'a']) current++;\n            res[i] = current++;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (tokenizer == null || !tokenizer.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokenizer = new StringTokenizer(reader.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokenizer.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    static int nextInt() throws IOException {\n        return Integer.parseInt(next());\n    }\n\n    static long nextLong() throws IOException {\n        return Long.parseLong(next());\n    }\n\n    static double nextDouble() throws IOException {\n        return Double.parseDouble(next());\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport itertools\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    idx = 0\n    a = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    b = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    l = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    r = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    \n    L = l - 1\n    R = r - 1\n    len_segment = R - L + 1\n\n    best = len_segment\n\n    for x in range(ord('a'), ord('z') + 1):\n        for y in range(ord('a'), ord('z') + 1):\n            for z in range(ord('a'), ord('z') + 1):\n                pattern = [chr(x), chr(y), chr(z)]\n                distinct_count = calculate_distinct(a, b, L, R, pattern)\n                if distinct_count < best:\n                    best = distinct_count\n\n    print(best)\n\ndef calculate_distinct(a, b, L, R, pat):\n    period = a + b\n    base = [''] * (3 * period)\n    \n    for idx in range(3):\n        prefix = generate_prefix(base, idx * period, a)\n        for i in range(a):\n            base[idx * period + i] = prefix[i]\n        for i in range(a, period):\n            base[idx * period + i] = pat[idx]\n\n    start = L % period\n    window_size = R - L + 1\n    segment = [''] * window_size\n    \n    # Copy from base starting at start position\n    for i in range(window_size):\n        if start + i < len(base):\n            segment[i] = base[start + i]\n        else:\n            # This case shouldn't happen given the logic, but just in case\n            segment[i] = 'a'\n\n    seen = [False] * 26\n    for c in segment:\n        if 'a' <= c <= 'z':\n            seen[ord(c) - ord('a')] = True\n\n    distinct = sum(1 for s in seen if s)\n    return distinct\n\ndef generate_prefix(buffer, offset, length):\n    used = [False] * 26\n    # Check characters already in buffer in the range [offset - length, offset - 1]\n    for i in range(offset - 1, offset - length - 1, -1):\n        if i >= 0 and i < len(buffer) and buffer[i] != '':\n            char_code = ord(buffer[i]) - ord('a')\n            if 0 <= char_code < 26:\n                used[char_code] = True\n\n    res = [''] * length\n    current = 0  # corresponds to 'a'\n    for i in range(length):\n        while current < 26 and used[current]:\n            current += 1\n        if current < 26:\n            res[i] = chr(ord('a') + current)\n            current += 1\n        else:\n            res[i] = 'a'  # fallback if all letters used\n    return res\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.686121585313231e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.2291887944447808e-05, -0.001870788517408073, -0.005930683575570583, -0.01604197360575199, -0.3615134060382843, -0.026313915848731995, -0.012978016398847103, -0.9068115949630737, -1.4662635294371285e-05, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.0016798973083496, -0.626502513885498, -7.748573807475623e-06, -0.06217386946082115, -8.702239938429557e-06, -0.0008499585674144328, -0.00041321321623399854, -0.0006329201860353351, -0.00021109737281221896, -5.602820692729438e-06, -0.49218934774398804, -2.264974000354414e-06, -0.0002961912250611931, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.523213803768158, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.06197534501552582, -5.364403477869928e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.005368578247725964, -8.34461570775602e-06, -9.60780744208023e-05, -3.6954811548639555e-06, 0.0, -4.6491513785440475e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.2159273865108844e-05, -4.172316494077677e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -5.006777428206988e-06, -6.723177648382261e-05, -3.576272320060525e-06, -5.364403477869928e-06, 0.0, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.38687530159950256, -0.00037865620106458664, -1.311301275563892e-06, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -1.3589766240329482e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.11291786283254623, -1.2755313036905136e-05, -0.0009190387791022658, 0.0, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -0.03555159270763397, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -9.572047565598041e